## ISS-018: web-admin package.json declares fake built-in dependencies

### File
`/root/Redball/web-admin/package.json`

### Original
```json
  "dependencies": {
    "bcryptjs": "^3.0.3",
    "child_process": "^1.0.2",
    "express": "^5.2.1",
    "fs": "^0.0.1-security",
    "jsonwebtoken": "^9.0.3",
    "node-pty": "^1.1.0",
    "path": "^0.12.7",
    "tail": "^2.2.6",
    "ws": "^8.20.0"
  },
```

### Replacement
```json
  "dependencies": {
    "bcryptjs": "^3.0.3",
    "express": "^5.2.1",
    "jsonwebtoken": "^9.0.3",
    "node-pty": "^1.1.0",
    "tail": "^2.2.6",
    "ws": "^8.20.0"
  },
```

### Reason
`fs`, `path`, and `child_process` are Node.js built-ins. The npm packages with the same names are placeholders and introduce supply-chain risk.

### Verification
After applying, run `npm install` to regenerate `package-lock.json`, then `node -c server.js` and `npm test`.
